      "content": "Their distrust of law enforcement would be deeply ingrained, stemming from historical patterns of systemic oppression against their community. They wouldn't view the police as neutral arbiters of law, but as an occupying force or an extension of a hostile power structure. This would manifest as extreme caution, a tendency to rely on informal, community-based networks for intelligence, and a deep-seated refusal to cooperate with outsiders. Their survival instinct would be rooted in protecting their people from the state, not just protecting their money.",
